    "title": "UPAWS pauses dog intake after emergency influx of 16 rescues - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By TV6 News Team ,\n14 hours ago SANDS TOWNSHIP, Mich. (WLUC) - The Upper Peninsula Animal Welfare Shelter announced Wednesday that it will be unable to take in surrendered or stray dogs until further notice. A post on the UPAWS Facebook page says that they received an emergency intake of 16 large dogs on Tuesday, as well as additional cats, from a potential neglect case. Read full article",
